{"title":"2020 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Properties of Logarithms)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Change_of_Base_Formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Change of Base Formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Observations)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Observations)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Solution_3_but_More_Detailed)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Solution 3 but More Detailed)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyOfMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyOfMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Sohil_Rathi\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Sohil Rathi</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/5/c0583fc535d0f034dc7812441bba87756a7aa5ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\log_2{6}+\\log_3{6}}?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/a/66afcdee6d28f171ff5786da6945be5fee66f9e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\sqrt{\\log_5{6}} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\sqrt{\\log_2{3}}+\\sqrt{\\log_3{2}} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\sqrt{\\log_2{6}}+\\sqrt{\\log_3{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"675\" height=\"22\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Properties_of_Logarithms.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Properties_of_Logarithms)\">Solution 1 (Properties of Logarithms)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Properties of Logarithms)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Recall that:\n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\">\n  <li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084b9a3cdd33d0c1fbe056e70f59ce4735dd0bab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_b{(uv)}=\\log_b u + \\log_b v.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"207\" height=\"20\" /></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/89541ae25001503db993f8fc7e786c17e40a9dd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_b u\\cdot\\log_u b=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"19\" /></li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p></ol>\n<p>We use these properties of logarithms to rewrite the original expression:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1055ea5ad7f686276266d0e017086f2bf327a857.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sqrt{\\log_2{6}+\\log_3{6}}&amp;=\\sqrt{(\\log_2{2}+\\log_2{3})+(\\log_3{2}+\\log_3{3})} \\\\ &amp;=\\sqrt{2+\\log_2{3}+\\log_3{2}} \\\\ &amp;=\\sqrt{\\left(\\sqrt{\\log_2{3}}+\\sqrt{\\log_3{2}}\\right)^2} \\\\ &amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\sqrt{\\log_2{3}}+\\sqrt{\\log_3{2}}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"434\" height=\"152\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM (Solution)\n</p><p>~JHawk0224 (Proposal)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Change_of_Base_Formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Change_of_Base_Formula)\">Solution 2 (Change of Base Formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Change of Base Formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f0949839ce59d0e6cdb1ad0577b924b8ed87e940.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\log_2{6}+\\log_3{6}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\log{6}}{\\log{2}} + \\frac{\\log{6}}{\\log{3}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\log{6}\\cdot\\log{3} + \\log{6}\\cdot\\log{2}}{\\log{3}\\cdot\\log{2}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\log{6}(\\log 2 + \\log 3)}{\\log 2\\cdot \\log 3}}.\\]\" width=\"697\" height=\"54\" />\nFrom here, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/b/d9baa783557b8e3933d155b235d07ab900a51cff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{\\frac{\\log{6}(\\log 2 + \\log 3)}{\\log 2\\cdot \\log 3}} &amp;= \\sqrt{\\frac{(\\log 2 + \\log 3)(\\log 2 + \\log 3)}{\\log 2\\cdot \\log 3}} &amp;= \\sqrt{\\frac{(\\log 2 + \\log 3)^2}{\\log 2\\cdot \\log 3}} &amp;= \\frac{\\log 2}{\\sqrt{\\log 2\\cdot\\log 3}} + \\frac{\\log 3}{\\sqrt{\\log 2\\cdot\\log 3}} \\\\ &amp;= \\sqrt{\\frac{\\log 2}{\\log 3}} + \\sqrt{\\frac{\\log 3}{\\log 2}} \\\\ &amp;= \\sqrt{\\log_3 2} + \\sqrt{\\log_2 3}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"848\" height=\"142\" />\nAnswer: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1cca5b0fdc1484d3226e35a5b6007b74cf6fde3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\sqrt{\\log_2{3}}+\\sqrt{\\log_3{2}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"193\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Note that in this solution, even the most minor steps have been written out. On the actual test, this solution would be quite fast, and much of it could easily be done in your head.\n</p><p>~ TheBeast5520\n</p><p>~ LeonidasTheConquerer (removed unnecessary steps)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Observations.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Observations)\">Solution 3 (Observations)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Observations)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the knowledge of the powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f885f96d2fb7e65f800de4ff71d7dcd0a5d2db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/6/c8631c318bc9c6cd0e1a47cbdad270d830ed5074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2{6}&gt;2.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/8552c09a4d0a8ca71a3fb8c1a946eee1d85bbd47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_3{6}&gt;1.5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a18f439786905da9ecd7595969c89a991c263013.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\log_2{6}+\\log_3{6}}&gt;\\sqrt{2.5+1.5}=2.\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"21\" /> Only choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> are greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1d1407aac4125d6c453a365eb173d96ebb48e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> is certainly incorrect: If we compare the squares of the original expression and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae69570c458db7421453f5388296ee0a31fb370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"17\" /> then they are clearly not equal. So, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/a/53ac9ea82abf3a0bf18dc5f0fe362e3126f80045.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\sqrt{\\log_2{3}}+\\sqrt{\\log_3{2}}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"194\" height=\"33\" /> \n</p><p>~Baolan\n</p><p>~Solasky (first edit on wiki!)\n</p><p>~chrisdiamond10\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (reformatted and merged the thoughts of all contributors)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Solution_3_but_More_Detailed.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Solution_3_but_More_Detailed)\">Solution 4 (Solution 3 but More Detailed)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Solution 3 but More Detailed)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: Only use this method if all else fails and you cannot find a way to simplify the logarithms.\n</p><p>We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/656c6f20868f997b54fcd9b24ded1d00b070a1b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/93032f1ab8b685d84a767a2fde0d9006a464b5e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> Additionally, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is halfway between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a35631e1e126934ead6d2af161e9d250827bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/2/7d2e5497d2fd16a18da58f6475061f823c4ed9eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"20\" /> knowing how exponents increase more the larger <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is, we can deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/656c6f20868f997b54fcd9b24ded1d00b070a1b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> is just above halfway between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/0/93032f1ab8b685d84a767a2fde0d9006a464b5e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> We can guesstimate this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef88f09b78d3bd9d3ec64819d2379270ecf705bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2{6} \\approx 2.55.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" /> (It's actually about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d04861b4c8c53350765ffe8de58a4a4c9328d162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.585.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />)\n</p><p>Next, we think of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5af1c99ec221e90b6d5fe7b70fe9c2dcb4f1bfd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_3{6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"19\" /> This is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e4797950b5e812b65381cbc5fc33ad2db5f57aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is halfway between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4ce0583e43880c5a6892f664bd95f9a34b53a5f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^1$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/436fdaa5de3a7564f796998e40c0feb18506db86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"18\" /> and similar to the logic for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb7b6454e1fd055e0876788ac1569d6bef5f3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2{6},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"19\" /> we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f1ef5eec9a260cd4f38fe439459a8274c89158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_3{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> is just above halfway between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e4797950b5e812b65381cbc5fc33ad2db5f57aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> We guesstimate this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c374ba133067e4e647997effa59af8b74c69980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_3{6} \\approx 1.55.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" /> (It's actually about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a17620f7b93a75e9b72f1c139fbb162c729bbb95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.631.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />)\n</p><p>So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d11cb8a4c5815d1a5d371bc3aae9dd7918032936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2{6} + \\log_3{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"19\" /> is approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee2c7d37ba3505a49bbda237016044e81cdc29d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4.1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> The square root of that is just above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1d1407aac4125d6c453a365eb173d96ebb48e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> maybe <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c883eaa34a6079d07e9cef9020d375d5b7a3859.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.02.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> We cross out all choices below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> since they are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1d1407aac4125d6c453a365eb173d96ebb48e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> can't possibly be true unless either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/656c6f20868f997b54fcd9b24ded1d00b070a1b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> and/or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/f/e3f1ef5eec9a260cd4f38fe439459a8274c89158.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_3{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (You can prove this by squaring.). Thus, the only feasible answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/a/53ac9ea82abf3a0bf18dc5f0fe362e3126f80045.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } \\sqrt{\\log_2{3}}+\\sqrt{\\log_3{2}}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"194\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>~PureSwag\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ObLQiTVxLco\">https://youtu.be/ObLQiTVxLco</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p>(This solution is wrong as it involves an identity that is not true ~pengf)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyOfMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyOfMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyOfMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0xgTR3UEqbQ\">https://youtu.be/0xgTR3UEqbQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Sohil_Rathi\">Video Solution by Sohil Rathi</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Sohil Rathi\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RdIIEhsbZKw?t=1463\">https://youtu.be/RdIIEhsbZKw?t=1463</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GmUWIXXf_uk?t=1298\">https://youtu.be/GmUWIXXf_uk?t